Description: softisp: stop the AGC below analogue gain 1.0, not below the lowest gain code
 again10 marks the point where the AGC stops trimming analogue gain and
 starts trimming exposure. It was initialised with camHelper_->gain(1.0),
 but gain() converts a gain *code*, so this asked for the gain of code 1 —
 the very bottom of the sensor's range — rather than a gain of 1.0.
 .
 The AGC therefore drove the gain all the way to its minimum before it
 would shorten exposure. Near the bottom of the range one gain code is a
 large relative step: on an OV5693 (codes 1..127, helper scale code/16)
 the AGC settled around 0.33 and a single step moved it by ~19%, far more
 than the +-0.2 MSV hysteresis band. The loop could never land inside the
 band and oscillated between steps, which is visible as the picture
 pulsing in brightness whenever a bright source such as a window is in
 frame. Exposure, which has thousands of fine steps, was pinned at its
 maximum the whole time and never used.
 .
 With the floor at a gain of 1.0 the AGC reduces gain to unity and then
 trims exposure, where the steps are fine enough to converge.
Author: Fil Dunsky
Bug: measured on a Surface Pro 8, OV5693 front camera, libcamera 0.7.0
Forwarded: no
Last-Update: 2026-09-01
--- a/src/ipa/simple/soft_simple.cpp
+++ b/src/ipa/simple/soft_simple.cpp
@@ -5,6 +5,7 @@
  * Simple Software Image Processing Algorithm module
  */
 
+#include <algorithm>
 #include <chrono>
 #include <stdint.h>
 #include <sys/mman.h>
@@ -227,7 +228,18 @@
 	if (camHelper_) {
 		context_.configuration.agc.againMin = camHelper_->gain(againMin);
 		context_.configuration.agc.againMax = camHelper_->gain(againMax);
-		context_.configuration.agc.again10 = camHelper_->gain(1.0);
+		/*
+		 * again10 is the analogue gain of 1.0: the point below which
+		 * the AGC stops trimming gain and starts trimming exposure.
+		 * gain() converts a gain *code*, so gain(1.0) returned the
+		 * gain of code 1, that is the very bottom of the sensor's
+		 * range. That let the AGC drive the gain down to its minimum
+		 * before touching exposure, into the region where one code is
+		 * a large relative step, and the loop oscillated there.
+		 */
+		context_.configuration.agc.again10 =
+			std::clamp(1.0, context_.configuration.agc.againMin,
+				   context_.configuration.agc.againMax);
 		context_.configuration.agc.againMinStep =
 			(context_.configuration.agc.againMax -
 			 context_.configuration.agc.againMin) /
